New Caledonia’s 19th government formally took office on Wednesday after its 11 members unanimously agreed on the allocation of portfolios, with the immediate task of securing €109 million by the end of August to avoid a complete shutdown of the local administration.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9650e24-90ce-11f1-9fd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3MC9WM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9650e24-90ce-11f1-9fd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3MC9WM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0721baa6-90cf-11f1-be84-e9eaf3a775e3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 06:00:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9650e24-90ce-11f1-9fd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3MC9WM.jpg">AFP - DELPHINE MAYEUR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ex-French PM Attal targeted by Russian 'interference' ahead of 2027 vote</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260805-ex-french-pm-attal-targeted-by-russian-interference-ahead-of-2027-vote</link><description>
Gabriel Attal, France’s former prime minister and Renaissance party leader, has been targeted by “foreign interference originating in Russia”, in the latest in a series of Kremlin‑linked operations aimed at destabilising the 2027 presidential election.
